- But any robot k in that range also removes up to R[k], so closure is:
    reach = max over chained intervals.
Since intervals are contiguous in sorted order, we can repeatedly extend:
    cur = p
    scan k from i+1 while k < cur: cur = max(cur, R[k])
A direct scan is too slow.
Observe:
    R[i] = max( p, max_{k in [i+1, p-1]} R[k] )
If that max exceeds p, closure continues automatically because those R[k] already include further chaining.
So we need range maximum of R on suffix already computed.
Use a segment tree for range max while processing i from N-1 down to 0.

After R[i] is known, count possible remaining sets.
Consider robots from index i onward.
At position i:
- either keep robot i forever: then move to i+1
- or activate robot i (possibly via Takahashi directly at some point): then robots [i, R[i)-1] disappear, move to R[i]
These choices are independent in DP:
    dp[i] = dp[i+1] + dp[R[i]]
Base dp[N] = 1.
Answer dp[0].

Why this counts distinct remaining sets:
For the leftmost remaining/removed undecided robot i, either it remains, or it is removed.
If removed, due to closure from activating i, exactly the whole block [i, R[i)-1] can be forced removed before touching later robots.
Thus every achievable final set corresponds uniquely to these choices.

Complexities:
O(N log N)
*/

public class Main {
    static final long MOD = 998244353L;

    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        long nextLong() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
            } while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);
            long sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }
            long val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            return (int) nextLong();
        }
    }

    static class SegTreeMax {
        int n;
        int[] seg;

        SegTreeMax(int size) {
            n = 1;
            while (n < size) n <<= 1;
            seg = new int[n << 1];
        }

        void set(int idx, int val) {
            int p = idx + n;
            seg[p] = val;
            p >>= 1;
            while (p > 0) {
                seg[p] = Math.max(seg[p << 1], seg[p << 1 | 1]);
                p >>= 1;
            }
        }

        int query(int l, int r) { // max on [l, r)
            if (l >= r) return 0;
            int res = 0;
            l += n;
            r += n;
            while (l < r) {
                if ((l & 1) == 1) res = Math.max(res, seg[l++]);
                if ((r & 1) == 1) res = Math.max(res, seg[--r]);
                l >>= 1;
                r >>= 1;
            }
            return res;
        }
    }

    static int lowerBound(long[] a, long key) {
        int l = 0, r = a.length;
        while (l < r) {
            int m = (l + r) >>> 1;
            if (a[m] >= key) r = m;
            else l = m + 1;
        }
        return l;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);
        int N = fs.nextInt();

        long[][] robots = new long[N][2];
        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            robots[i][0] = fs.nextLong();
            robots[i][1] = fs.nextLong();
        }

        Arrays.sort(robots, Comparator.comparingLong(a -> a[0]));

        long[] X = new long[N];
        long[] D = new long[N];
        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            X[i] = robots[i][0];
            D[i] = robots[i][1];
        }

        int[] R = new int[N];
        SegTreeMax st = new SegTreeMax(N);

        for (int i = N - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            long reachPos = X[i] + D[i];
            int p = lowerBound(X, reachPos);
            int mx = st.query(i + 1, p);
            R[i] = Math.max(p, mx);
            st.set(i, R[i]);
        }

        long[] dp = new long[N + 1];
        dp[N] = 1;
        for (int i = N - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            dp[i] = dp[i + 1] + dp[R[i]];
            if (dp[i] >= MOD) dp[i] -= MOD;
        }

        System.out.println(dp[0] % MOD);
    }
}
